WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.590
All right, well, you
know, I love the holidays.

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:03.520
You know that about me.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.353
I love the holidays.

00:00:04.353 --> 00:00:05.400
And a big part of Christmas, folks,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.680
is well, spending time
with your loved ones.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.097
For me, that's Andy Richter
here, sitting next to me.

00:00:09.097 --> 00:00:10.046
Aw, come on.

00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:10.879
(studio audience applauds)

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:11.712
It is.

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:12.545
Golly.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.378
It is.

00:00:13.378 --> 00:00:15.103
You know, Andy and I have
become very good friends

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:17.650
in the three seasons that
we've been doing this show.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.483
[Andy] Right.

00:00:18.483 --> 00:00:19.890
And we decided, actually recently,

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.800
that I should get to
know Andy even better.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.410
And Andy should take me to Chicago

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.830
and look around his old neighborhood.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.510
Andy Richter Chicago.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.343
[Andy] Right.

00:00:28.343 --> 00:00:29.176
Sort of some of your old haunts.

00:00:29.176 --> 00:00:30.009
Yeah.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:30.910
Well, we did that last night on the show,

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:31.743
we took a camera crew.

00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:32.576
Yeah.

00:00:32.576 --> 00:00:33.409
We went to Chicago.

00:00:33.409 --> 00:00:34.242
You showed me around.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:35.578
I think we visited 85 bars,

00:00:35.578 --> 00:00:37.290
and we had a good time.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.123
[Andy] Yes.

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:38.956
We really did.

00:00:38.956 --> 00:00:39.789
[Andy] As far as we know.

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:40.622
That's right.

00:00:40.622 --> 00:00:41.455
Well, tonight,

00:00:41.455 --> 00:00:42.339
tonight is part two

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:44.460
of the installment.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.010
Well, this where we went,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.850
I was wondering who was living
in my old apartment now.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:49.840
You know,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.940
and most people couldn't
just go ring on the bell,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.370
but when you bring a camera crew.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.338
You can get away with stuff, right.

00:00:55.338 --> 00:00:56.171
You can.

00:00:56.171 --> 00:00:58.244
So Andy and I went to
where you used to live,

00:00:58.244 --> 00:00:59.952
and this really happened.

00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:04.050
We just rang the bell and
things unfolded, as they say.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.930
Let's take a look now at
our visit to Andy's old pad

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:08.763
in Chicago.

00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:09.596
Take a look.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.290
All right, Conan, this is
the apartment I lived at.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.520
Oh, it's nice, it's really nice.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.700
Yeah, I have no idea who lives there now.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.790
This is sort of, Lincoln
had his log cabin,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.470
and you started out in
this humble apartment.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.148
Right here on Cullom Street in Chicago.

00:01:25.148 --> 00:01:25.981
All right.

00:01:25.981 --> 00:01:27.189
So I thought we'd just ring the buzzer

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:28.840
and see who's there.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.550
Do you know, you don't
know these people at all?

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.383
No, I have no idea.

00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:33.460
All right, let's just ring
it and see what happens.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.293
Okay.

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:36.960
(buzzer buzzes)

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.510
I hope they're home.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.343
Yeah.

00:01:40.343 --> 00:01:41.176
(intercom clicks)

00:01:41.176 --> 00:01:42.009
[Julie] Who is it?

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:44.610
Hi, it's Andy Richter and Conan O'Brien

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.076
from "Late Night with Conan O'Brien."

00:01:47.076 --> 00:01:49.700
I used to live here and we're wondering

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.780
if we could come up with a video tape crew

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.683
and film the apartment.

00:01:54.623 --> 00:01:57.010
[Julie] I'm sorry, right
now wouldn't be a good time.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:57.980
Now?

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.275
How come?

00:01:59.275 --> 00:02:00.287
[Julie] I have guests.

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:02.350
Um, could I talk to her?

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.183
[Andy] Yeah.

00:02:03.183 --> 00:02:04.440
[Conan] Ma'am, Ma'am?

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.424
I don't think you understand.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.900
This is Conan O'Brien talking now,

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.269
that was Andy Richter.

00:02:09.269 --> 00:02:10.102
(studio audience laughs)

00:02:10.102 --> 00:02:10.935
It would really be great.

00:02:10.935 --> 00:02:12.640
We came all the way from New York City

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.180
and it'll just take a second.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:17.500
We'll just, you know, see
where Andy used to live.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.109
And it'll just take a
second, I promise you.

00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:22.690
(silence)

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.220
Well, I think I've pretty
much got her on the ropes.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.220
I think she's about to give in.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:26.770
Yeah, hello?

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:27.610
Hello?

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.920
[Andy] I bet they're coming
to the window to look at us.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.753
[Conan] You think?

00:02:30.753 --> 00:02:31.586
Hello?

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.610
Now wouldn't be a good time.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.193
Now wouldn't be a good time.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.831
[Andy] When can we come?

00:02:39.831 --> 00:02:40.664
(studio audience titters)

00:02:40.664 --> 00:02:41.834
[Conan] Are they turning lights out?

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:42.810
[Julie] Back up from the door.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:43.643
[Andy] What?

00:02:43.643 --> 00:02:44.476
[Conan] What?

00:02:44.476 --> 00:02:45.892
[Julie] Back up from the door.

00:02:45.892 --> 00:02:47.660
[Conan] Back up from the door, okay.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.050
[Andy] See, it's really us.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:49.883
It's us.

00:02:49.883 --> 00:02:50.716
Can you see us?

00:02:50.716 --> 00:02:51.780
Back up more.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.613
Hello?

00:02:52.613 --> 00:02:53.720
Hello?

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.411
Are you peeking through the blinds?

00:02:55.411 --> 00:02:57.170
(studio audience laughs)

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.070
We're on after Leno.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.546
(studio audience laughs and applauds)

00:03:01.546 --> 00:03:02.907
It's "Must See TV."

00:03:03.951 --> 00:03:04.784
Hello?

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.053
Can you see us?

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.506
We're really are who we say we are.

00:03:10.506 --> 00:03:11.339
(studio audience laughs)

00:03:11.339 --> 00:03:13.373
Yeah, we're not just
celebrity impersonators.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.653
Although boy, what a sad
celebrity impersonating pair

00:03:18.653 --> 00:03:20.120
that would be!

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.210
[Andy] You'll be on national television.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:25.229
[Conan] Yeah, there might
even be some money in it.

00:03:25.229 --> 00:03:26.062
(studio audience laughs)

00:03:26.062 --> 00:03:26.895
[Julie] Come on in.

00:03:26.895 --> 00:03:27.728
All right.

00:03:27.728 --> 00:03:28.615
Oh, cool.

00:03:28.615 --> 00:03:29.498
(studio laughs and applauds)

00:03:29.498 --> 00:03:31.940
See that, they're on
national television got them.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.236
I think I mentioned money.

00:03:33.236 --> 00:03:34.069
[Andy] Oh, you did?

00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:34.902
Yeah.

00:03:34.902 --> 00:03:35.735
Hi there!

00:03:35.735 --> 00:03:36.568
Hi, I'm Andy.

00:03:36.568 --> 00:03:37.401
Hi Andy!

00:03:37.401 --> 00:03:38.234
Hi, nice to meet you.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.158
Your name is? - I'm Julie.

00:03:39.158 --> 00:03:39.991
Hi Julie. - Hi.

00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:41.566
Couldn't you have called
first or something?

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:42.399
[Conan] It's better this way.

00:03:42.399 --> 00:03:43.523
[Andy] That's the whole point.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.506
[Conan] This is the way
Ed McMahon does it on TV.

00:03:45.506 --> 00:03:46.370
(studio audience titters)

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.870
I didn't win a million
dollars or anything?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.836
[Conan] No, no.

00:03:48.836 --> 00:03:50.598
This is, the only difference
is he gives a million dollars

00:03:50.598 --> 00:03:52.380
and there might be a 20 in it for you,

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.323
or something with us.

00:03:53.323 --> 00:03:54.460
You're probably just
gonna criticize, like,

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.990
the bathroom's not clean
and stuff like that.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:56.823
[Andy] No, not at all.

00:03:56.823 --> 00:03:57.656
[Conan] Cool idea, let's go.

00:03:57.656 --> 00:03:59.090
[Andy] Can we come in?

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.370
They've done the bathroom really nice.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.014
It was a dump before.

00:04:02.014 --> 00:04:03.740
[Conan] This is nice.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:04.573
Yeah.

00:04:04.573 --> 00:04:05.406
Look at this.

00:04:05.406 --> 00:04:07.000
This actually worked out really well.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.941
Look, it's their little toilet elf.

00:04:08.941 --> 00:04:11.110
(Conan and studio audience laugh)

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.322
[Conan] It's always
there when you need him.

00:04:13.322 --> 00:04:14.155
(studio audience laughs and applauds)

00:04:14.155 --> 00:04:15.600
Actually, I kicked through this door once.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.160
Not this door, but it was another door,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.540
and I kicked through it.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.330
We're just getting these weird flashes

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.710
of what your life was once like.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.290
This room is littered with empties,

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.123
ladies and gentlemen.

00:04:25.123 --> 00:04:26.097
It's Chicago.

00:04:26.097 --> 00:04:26.930
(Conan laughs)

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.763
I guess that's just --

00:04:27.763 --> 00:04:28.680
It's the holidays.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.640
Yeah, look, what's going on here?

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.270
It's just, there's something.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:33.103
You have a problem,

00:04:33.103 --> 00:04:34.098
you realize that, don't you?

00:04:34.098 --> 00:04:35.110
Yep.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:36.410
We're here to help you.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:37.710
Bottles are all over the place

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.070
and none in the refrigerator.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.020
Here. (Conan laughs)

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:40.853
Look at this!

00:04:40.853 --> 00:04:41.686
(studio audience laughs)

00:04:41.686 --> 00:04:43.170
This is the kind of
thing you get awards for,

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.189
in Chicago.

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:45.022
(Conan and studio audience laugh)

00:04:45.022 --> 00:04:45.930
(studio audience applauds)

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.969
[Conan] Is there a picture
here, anywhere, of your fiance?

00:04:47.969 --> 00:04:48.802
Yeah, there's one right here.

00:04:48.802 --> 00:04:49.963
[Conan] Could we see a
picture of him, please?

00:04:49.963 --> 00:04:50.796
Mm hmm.

00:04:50.796 --> 00:04:51.629
[Andy] Oh, he's a very handsome man.

00:04:51.629 --> 00:04:52.462
[Conan] He's a handsome guy.

00:04:52.462 --> 00:04:53.350
You make a very handsome couple.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.183
[Julie] Well, thank you.

00:04:54.183 --> 00:04:55.490
Oh, I am having people coming over,

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:56.900
so that's why the place is at least

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.600
in somewhat decent order.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.680
Wow, and what a
conversation piece that is.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.513
[Conan] Oh!

00:05:01.513 --> 00:05:02.346
Oh, Andy.

00:05:02.346 --> 00:05:03.350
Oh, my God!

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:04.580
[Conan] Andy, no!

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.200
Tell me it's not broken.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.080
[Conan] Andy, it's fine.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:09.913
[Andy] Oh!

00:05:09.913 --> 00:05:11.120
Everything's fine, ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.847
[Andy] Look, it's still
intact, just like their love.

00:05:13.847 --> 00:05:15.390
(studio audience cheers and applauds)

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.500
Hey, you knew --

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.900
look, she knew we were coming

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:18.733
Oh!

00:05:18.733 --> 00:05:19.822
And she baked, I think those are quiches,

00:05:19.822 --> 00:05:21.110
if I'm not mistaken.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:24.610
No, that's a Chicago
delicacy called Baco Pie.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.630
Made with Bacos.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:26.463
Is that true?

00:05:26.463 --> 00:05:27.296
Yeah.

00:05:27.296 --> 00:05:28.129
Is that a Baco Pie, ma'am?

00:05:28.129 --> 00:05:29.870
[Julie] No, it's sun dried tomato quiche.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:30.754
Wow, excellent.

00:05:30.754 --> 00:05:31.587
(studio audience titters)

00:05:31.587 --> 00:05:33.040
I know what I'm talking about.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:33.873
Very nice.

00:05:33.873 --> 00:05:34.916
Thank you for those, I appreciate it.

00:05:34.916 --> 00:05:36.230
We'll take those on the way out.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.580
Was there a piano here,
when you were here, Andy?

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.060
No, no piano.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.093
You, you play the piano, is that right?

00:05:41.093 --> 00:05:42.307
[Julie] I play a little bit.

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:43.850
[Conan] Can you play
us a little something?

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:45.340
Okay, are we ready?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.173
Let's go.

00:05:46.173 --> 00:05:47.290
I believe we're ready.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.410
[Conan] Okay.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.023
(Julie plays three
chords of "Jingle Bells")

00:05:50.023 --> 00:05:51.011
Come on, you're supposed to sing.

00:05:51.011 --> 00:05:51.844
No, no, that's just the introduction.

00:05:51.844 --> 00:05:52.677
No, it's not.

00:05:52.677 --> 00:05:53.974
Jingle bells.

00:05:53.974 --> 00:05:55.001
Okay, wow, here we go.

00:05:55.001 --> 00:05:55.834
Okay. Wow.

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.204
Okay.

00:05:57.204 --> 00:05:59.116
♪ Jingle bells ♪

00:05:59.116 --> 00:06:01.271
♪ Jingle bells ♪

00:06:01.271 --> 00:06:03.940
♪ Jingle all the way ♪

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.538
Why aren't you singing?

00:06:05.538 --> 00:06:06.371
Because I'm playing.

00:06:06.371 --> 00:06:09.213
♪ Oh what fun it is to ride ♪

00:06:09.213 --> 00:06:11.200
♪ On a one horse open sleigh ♪

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.150
In a one horse --

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.241
♪ Sleigh, hey ♪

00:06:13.241 --> 00:06:15.192
♪ Hey, back off, man. ♪

00:06:15.192 --> 00:06:20.192
(studio audience laughs, cheers, applauds)

00:06:20.732 --> 00:06:25.232
Hey, you guys think you
wanna play some board games?

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:27.613
I think we're all right.

00:06:27.613 --> 00:06:28.462
Yeah, I'm all right.

00:06:28.462 --> 00:06:29.384
Yeah, we're okay.

00:06:29.384 --> 00:06:30.217
All right.

00:06:34.568 --> 00:06:36.566
(studio audience laughs)

00:06:36.566 --> 00:06:38.300
(chatter from TV show)

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.133
Beer?

00:06:43.487 --> 00:06:44.616
(studio audience laughs)

00:06:44.616 --> 00:06:47.116
(door knocks)

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.033
Hi.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.200
Hey, hi, how are you, Christian?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.033
Jesus, what's up?

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:52.187
Hi, how are you?

00:06:52.187 --> 00:06:53.020
Not much, this is Andy.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:53.853
Hi, Christian.

00:06:53.853 --> 00:06:54.686
Hey, you're here.

00:06:54.686 --> 00:06:55.545
I heard a lot about you.

00:06:55.545 --> 00:06:57.430
Julie, thanks again.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.360
Hi, nice to see you again.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.193
How are you?

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.460
Listen, basically,

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.670
well, Andy explained,

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:06.460
we were here last night
and you were very nice

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.640
to have us and let us in.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.610
Thank you.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:10.443
Yeah, basically,

00:07:10.443 --> 00:07:11.900
so we thought --

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.520
Since you were so nice
that we would come back

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.840
with a surprise for you.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.460
A big surprise.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:20.730
And, so that's what we
want to do right now.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:21.573
So here it is,

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.910
Here he is.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.500
Oh, hey, how you doing?

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.883
[Conan] Jerry Springer.

00:07:26.883 --> 00:07:31.802
(studio audience cheers and applauds)

00:07:31.802 --> 00:07:33.018
♪ Jingle bells ♪

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:35.042
♪ Jingle bells ♪

00:07:35.042 --> 00:07:38.973
♪ Jingle all the way ♪

00:07:38.973 --> 00:07:42.264
♪ Oh what fun it is to ride ♪

00:07:42.264 --> 00:07:46.540
♪ On a one horse open sleigh, hey ♪

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.340
We thought it might be nice,
Jerry, since you're here,

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.863
if you could end things
with a final thought.

00:07:50.863 --> 00:07:52.255
(studio audience titters)

00:07:52.255 --> 00:07:53.088
(audience member hoots)

00:07:53.088 --> 00:07:56.280
Well, I guess I want to say that,

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.783
for those of us in Chicago,

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:01.388
there are fewer things
that we're more proud of

00:08:01.388 --> 00:08:06.388
than to see Andy make it so
big in the world of television,

00:08:07.126 --> 00:08:09.970
in the world of entertainment.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:12.003
And to see you come back to your roots,

00:08:13.216 --> 00:08:16.560
it kinda makes us all feel
a little bit, you know,

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.160
we well up in our eyes
thinking of you, Andy.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.768
What you've done, and--

00:08:20.768 --> 00:08:21.602
(studio audience laughs
and applauds lightly)

00:08:21.602 --> 00:08:22.435
You all right?

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.095
Yeah.

00:08:24.095 --> 00:08:27.920
But America should know
that with Andy and Conan

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.963
here in Chicago on this night,

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.922
New York has never been safer.

00:08:33.922 --> 00:08:35.936
(studio audience laughs and applauds)

00:08:35.936 --> 00:08:38.160
That's a really nice
thought, thank you very much.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.660
Tell them to stay in school.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:48.700
Kids, Andy said it best
when he said stay in school.

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:58.029
(studio audience cheers
and applauds lightly)

00:08:58.029 --> 00:09:01.362
(tortilla chips crunch)

00:09:14.564 --> 00:09:17.530
(studio audience cheers and applauds)

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:18.668
It was nice to go back.

00:09:18.668 --> 00:09:19.501
Wow.

00:09:21.373 --> 00:09:22.582
Merry Christmas, Andy.

00:09:22.582 --> 00:09:23.840
Merry Christmas.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:24.859
All right, folks.

00:09:24.859 --> 00:09:26.440
We're gonna take a quick break.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.480
I think we learned a lot there.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.680
Our thanks to Chicago, and
of course, Jerry Springer.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:31.620
When we come back, Kevin
Pollak's gonna be with us,

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:32.453
so stick around.

